Noam: Whoa! Are you in Costa Rica? What the *****

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Carmen Cruickshank: I know.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Carmen Cruickshank: I know. I wish I was in Costa Rica. I actually really like tropical stuff, but I'm in Northern Virginia, an hour away from DC, surprisingly. So it's just kind of like humid today. So I don't know. I live outside.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Noam: Oh, okay.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Noam: Did you… were you… were you just on the website of Sunny?

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yes.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Noam: Okay, so I get, like, uh…

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mmhm.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Noam: I get, like, alerts to tell me that a visitor is on the website, and I saw someone from that area, I was like, hmm, I wonder if that's where they're located.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, that's where I come from. But yeah, are you —.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Noam: I'm sorry, I'm not at home, and I'm in the car because I had to run out for errands, and I hope it's okay if you share the Google Ads page instead of me.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Thank you.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Perfectly fine, yeah, absolutely, that's what my plan was originally. Alright, and then you're in…

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Las Vegas or Southern California?

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:29.000
Noam: I'm in Los Angeles. Um, we do… we do serve… we serve all of, uh, Southern California, and also we can do, you know, whatever is a short flight away. We have, uh, rates for that as well, for Vegas, for San Francisco, Phoenix area, Arizona.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Hold on just a second.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Noam: Um, and we also had a couple of gigs, like, in Chicago and New York, so we do it anywhere in the United States, I would say.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yes.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yes.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:44.000
Noam: Um, but yeah, I'll tell you a little bit about the story of the business, if you want, like, to have a little bit of a background on what we do and who we are.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.000
Noam: Um…

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.000
Noam: I don't know if that's necessary or not. Okay.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:53.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, you could tell me a good summary. That'd be nice.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:09.000
Noam: Okay, so my husband and I are both immigrants. We moved to the U.S. from Israel. We started the business together, the band, after I worked and he worked for many different live entertainment companies. I did, like, sales and operations for them for a very long time, and he.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:24.000
Noam: also performs as a sax player, and we gain a lot of experience on stages here with the crowd, with the American crowd. And then we started our own thing a few years ago, and we slowly built the platform for it to become a business. Only a few months ago, I quit my job to do this full-time.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mmhm.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Nice.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:41.000
Noam: Um, so most of our good gigs until now, we got booked through the agency that I worked in, another talent agency, and we… we no longer get bookings from them. I really need, uh, leads, good leads, and until now, I've been doing.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:46.000
Noam: I got, like… I spent, I would say, maybe $2,000 on Meta ads.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:57.000
Noam: Um, in the past month and a half, I got maybe 80 leads or 70 leads, which is a good number. Most of them were trash, were, like.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Uh…

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:12.000
Noam: no budget, they had, like, $1500 to spend on a band, and… or 800 bucks budget, so I need… I needed to make an adjustment there, but I figured it doesn't work, so I shut it off, and then yesterday, I booked my first metal lead for a wedding this month, so…

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Wow.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:18.000
Noam: I'm like, okay, maybe I should turn it on again, I don't know, maybe I judged it too quickly.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:32.000
Noam: Um… but yeah, I need… I will get to Meta later on, because I think we do need to work on it, but for now, I wanted us to focus on the Google, um, ads, because it has brought me better quality leads, um…

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Bye-bye.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:41.000
Noam: I think the only difference is that they don't see my video right away, and the video is a selling point, the promo shoot that we use for the meta campaign, so…

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:57.000
Noam: I don't know if you'll have any insights about that, um… but yeah, anyway, this is where I'm at. I need help, I have a friend who built me the campaigns, and uh… we've been doing a lot of back and forth, it's been almost a month and a half, and only recently, that campaign started, like, generating.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:03.000
Noam: leads, I got incoming calls from a few clients, but I haven't booked anything from that campaign yet.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:08.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay, that makes sense. Yeah, that was very, very helpful background. And I think…

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.000
Noam: Funny.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:24.000
Carmen Cruickshank: That's what I noticed, though, is, of course, with Meta, is there's more leads, and normally it's lower quality, but there is a certain way you can, like… I don't want to say manipulate, but, like, change it to where you're getting higher quality. So, like, if you target people with the top 10% income or more, that can prevent, like, the low-b.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Uh, and then you have…

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:27.000
Noam: Oh, you can do that?

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:31.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, you can do that. You can do top 5%, top 10%, 20%.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.000
Noam: Really?

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:40.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, I would probably start with, like, yeah, like, top 20. I think that will just, like, cut out a lot of **** leads, if that makes sense.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.000
Noam: Okay, that's good to know.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:56.000
Noam: Yeah, well, I had only, like, a lot of quinceaneras, and I'm like, this is not the kind of band that performs in a quinceanera, with all due respect. Nor a bat mitzvah, you know, unless it is, like, a million dollar event, and they want to spend that money, but most of the events I got inquiries for were private events.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:14.000
Noam: and quinceaneras, some weddings, but those weddings also, they were, like, I think, I don't know, people on the spectrum left their details multiple times, and when I called, they don't know how to talk well. I feel like a lot of it is spam, too. I'm not sure how I get those leads, but yeah, it was very bad for a very long time, and now.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:20.000
Noam: I finally booked an event through Facebook, which is incredible.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:37.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, and it's funny because you would think it's Google first and then Meta, but it's like it was Meta, so it worked. But yeah, with Google though, it is higher quality leads. And so it's like also manipulating it to like get more of those because normally, of course, Meta is cheaper. There's more leads there, but like we can figure it out with Google.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.000
Noam: Yeah.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:41.000
Carmen Cruickshank: So, I'm gonna share my screen. There was, I think…

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.000
Noam: Okay.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:47.000
Noam: Did you say… I know I had multiple campaigns, but only one of them is active right now, which is the OG… the wedding's OG.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:53.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yes. Yes. Wedding's OG. I like the OG thing. That made it very clear immediately. Okay.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.000
Noam: I'll tell you why I…

00:05:53.000 --> 00:06:04.000
Noam: Hold it this way, because when I started to build a campaign, I did it with Claude, with AI. Um, I used Claude for Chrome, it built the whole campaign for me, and I was like, okay, I'm letting it run.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Uh-huh.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:08.000
Noam: Um, I went outside the country, and for 2 weeks, I got, like.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:25.000
Noam: I think within the first few weeks, I got 4 or 5 leads, and they were really good quality of people, and I was like, oh my god, it's working! But then my bot told me, you know what, you're wasting a lot of money during the times of the night, so we have to, like, limit the schedule, and while we're doing that, maybe also change a few negative words.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, thank you.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:31.000
Noam: And then it became ***** and it didn't work ever. So, this campaign is the same one.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:29.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:32.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mmhm.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:49.000
Noam: But I turned it off for a very long time, and I just recently turned it on again with some adjustments, with the help of my friend. And I want to know what he did, because he is from another country, I don't know if he's, like, very well familiar with the American, um, clientele, with the ones I'm aiming for, for a luxury market. I want to know…

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:59.000
Noam: English-wise, because it's my second language, if the keywords and the way we, like, use the headlines, if that's okay, if you think this is good enough, or those are the things we should change.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:58.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mmhm.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:08.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay. Yeah, that's good to know. I can definitely check that out. My computer's a little slow sometimes. I hope it's fast, but we'll see. Okay.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.000
Noam: Great.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:13.000
Carmen Cruickshank: So I'm just kind of curious, now that you said that, what changes…

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:17.000
Carmen Cruickshank: He made…

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:18.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:25.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay, yeah, he increased 20 to 30, which is good.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:30.000
Carmen Cruickshank: I see he, like, changed the copy.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.000
Carmen Cruickshank: And then… let's see…

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:38.000
Noam: Yeah, we did that a few days ago, because we looked at the…

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:49.000
Noam: headlines, and we looked at the recommendations of Google for new headlines. We made 2 changes, or 3 changes, something very minor, to try and see if it will, you know, get, uh…

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mmhm.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.000
Noam: Better conversion.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:56.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm. Yeah, that makes sense. Okay, so I'll just start with like…

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:12.000
Carmen Cruickshank: I have all these things, and so I don't want to like just like so I'll try to organize it. But basically going to the campaign level. So of course, I'm just gonna single out this one campaign. So $30 a day. I think that's pretty good. A lot of the people. Sometimes they get like.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.000
Noam: Okay.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:19.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Uh, they only want to do $10 a day, or sometimes just $14, and it really slows down the data, so the budget there is good.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:20.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Now you're clicking…

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:21.000
Noam: Okay, great.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:33.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm, I'm just gonna go based off also the past 30-ish days. Uh, click-through rate isn't bad, like, normally 3-5% is what we aim for, so just, that's the, you know, the percentage of people that see your ad and click.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:50.000
Carmen Cruickshank: cost per click is a little high. So of course, like with Meta, you're paying based on how many people see the ad with Google. It's how many people click on the ad. And so it is a little high. But it's only because we're on maximize conversions. So.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:38.000
Noam: Okay.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:09:06.000
Carmen Cruickshank: I normally have two types of campaigns. So there's the maximize clicks where I just tell Google, like, we just want clicks. And I do that to start just to get data and see how people interact with the website. Because if the website is good and well built to capture leads, it should work well.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:23.000
Carmen Cruickshank: And then once we get the good amount of clicks, Google knows the type of people that become a lead, and then they send that when you switch to maximize conversions. But Google will charge more per click when they're like, oh, okay, these are like high quality people and high quality leads. We're going to charge more for each click.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:16.000
Noam: Yeah.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:26.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Which can sometimes…

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:34.000
Carmen Cruickshank: hinder the account. Because if we are at $30 a day, then we can only really afford six clicks per day, which slows down the data a little bit.

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:43.000
Carmen Cruickshank: So I don't think it's an issue to keep it at maximize conversions because some of the changes that I'll suggest I think will help a lot. But if…

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:53.000
Carmen Cruickshank: this is just me, but, like, I'll start a campaign, and I'll start on maximize clicks, so that we get, like, the cheaper cost per click, all those… all the data, and then switch it. Uh, let's…

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:52.000
Noam: Yeah.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:10:03.000
Noam: I think I did that, but it didn't… it didn't produce any results. Um, I was told to do that for a little bit, and I think this campaign even, we had it for… on Mexico.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:57.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:13.000
Noam: But it didn't make it better for maximized conversion. I'm wondering if I should just delete all these campaigns and start from scratch, or give this shot like this one, if it's built well.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:05.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:24.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, I think some of the changes I'll suggest will help or clarify it because I feel like we could recover this and if we see it's not recovering, then we could start something new.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:24.000
Noam: Okay.

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:31.000
Carmen Cruickshank: But yeah, so as for conversions, I was looking at the conversion actions, or is it?

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:35.000
Carmen Cruickshank: And…

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:45.000
Carmen Cruickshank: So I saw Google is tracking 3 different conversions right now, so I know we got 4 phone calls from the ad, and then there's 2 separate, uh…

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:50.000
Carmen Cruickshank: conversion actions right now for submitting a lead form, which I don't know which one.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:11:03.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Google is using to track, uh, but I think just cleaning up the conversion tracking would help, so just having one singular submit lead form one, that way Google isn't tracking two at the same time if it's just one, if that makes sense.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:17.000
Noam: Yeah, it's basically changing the results for me, and it's showing me more conversions than what it really is. I knew I had that issue, because I had my bot check the campaign as well, and he said the same thing.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:04.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Like.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:12.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Exactly.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:22.000
Noam: Um, but I'm not sure… one is, like, it says Google Analytics.

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:23.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:38.000
Noam: It's because I wanted to know where the leads come, uh, to my, um, to my page when they leave their details and they fill out the form. I wanted to know where they came to me, if it was from Facebook, if it was from the Google Ads campaign, um…

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:43.000
Noam: And that is why I did it, because I had the Meta campaign running, and I guess the second one is…

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:48.000
Noam: Are they… do we have a way to know if they record the same contacts, the same forms?

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:58.000
Carmen Cruickshank: I think, for me, I don't really know exactly, I think it's only based on, like, assumption, really, but we can change that, so we can, like, delete a conversion action and just have one.

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:00.000
Noam: Okay.

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:03.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Uh, so I feel like that would fix it, and basically tell Google, like.

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:08.000
Carmen Cruickshank: we're not getting the actual results that you think we are, like we need to actually fix this.

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:14.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Um, I'm gonna go real quick into campaign settings and just make sure the campaign's optimized just for leads.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:19.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Do you like getting phone calls from ads or do you not like that?

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:23.000
Noam: Yeah, I love it. I think it's the hottest leads, because they're looking for something urgent.

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:24.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:28.000
Noam: And I'm a good closer, so I would love to have more phone calls.

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:43.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay, that's perfect, yeah. And then it's optimized for the lead forms and the phone calls, so that's great. And I'll just leave that there. Okay. And then the next thing I check is, of course, where they go. So, like, if the website is optimized for those conversions.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:13:01.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Then, of course, we're getting a cheaper cost per click. We don't have to increase the budget, all these things. And your website looks great, like, genuinely. I like how it starts off with, like, the promo video, like, you're there singing, all these beautiful things. And, um, it's very clear, too. Like, Los Angeles Wedding Jazz Band, I see so many people's websites.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:07.000
Noam: This is… this is not the website, this is a landing page that I built specifically for this Google campaign.

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:08.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yes, I meant to, like…

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:10.000
Noam: Because I, I, yeah.

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:17.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, I should have changed my words, because yeah, you can tell it's a landing page without the menu and everything, and that's good too, is you have that. Uh, something I did notice…

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:29.000
Carmen Cruickshank: that I think we could… only one small change I think we could make onto the site is to have more of these buttons more on mobile. On the website, I think we could maybe add one, like, here…

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.000
Noam: Mmhm.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Here…

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:35.000
Noam: Okay, even though you have the hovering button on the right bottom corner?

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:51.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, I know it sounds like it maybe is too much, but I think it would increase conversions because that's what I see most of the time. I think it's not as necessary on the computer because you do have a few throughout. I think it's more necessary on mobile because people have to scroll more for that button.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:41.000
Noam: Okay.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:53.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Because when I look at your…

00:13:53.000 --> 00:14:01.000
Carmen Cruickshank: When I see where your ad showed, so comparing it phones to computers.

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:10.000
Carmen Cruickshank: all our conversions came from the computer, even the phone call ones. And so, of course, they don't have to scroll as much to get it, but I think if we added those buttons on the phone.

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:13.000
Carmen Cruickshank: More, you'd probably see more.

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:12.000
Noam: Okay.

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:18.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, but overall it looks really good. It doesn't really do anything. Yeah.

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:16.000
Noam: Okay, that's, that's good.

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:25.000
Noam: Thank you. The landing page has, like, a good order, user experience, like, all these things?

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:19.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay.

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:32.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, I'd say so. I mean, it loaded pretty fast. I don't know why right now it's not loading because before when I checked it out, I saw the video.

