Noam: Okay. You don't think it's too pushy? I just… I don't know, I thought… I heard about it before someone mentioned it to me, and I thought maybe it's not, like, aiming the right, um… like, I'm trying to sell a luxury van, and I don't think it's, like, very much…

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:42.000
Carmen Cruickshank: But…

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:47.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:55.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mmhm.

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:55.000
Noam: You don't think…

00:15:55.000 --> 00:16:02.000
Noam: like, cheap to be like, well, here's what we do, comparing to others, don't do. I just… I don't know, it made me a little…

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:19.000
Carmen Cruickshank: like, icked out. Yeah, that makes sense. You could probably do it more from the angle of just, like, the unique stuff we offer, and maybe not compare other people. And I think in other people's minds, they're like, oh, like, that's unique, I don't see other people do that, and then we're not saying other people don't do that, you know? I think that'd be…

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:05.000
Noam: I think it was too much, yeah.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:11.000
Noam: Mmhm.

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:17.000
Noam: Yes.

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:20.000
Noam: Okay.

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:22.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Angle. But yeah, overall though, like…

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:23.000
Noam: That's a good angle.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:36.000
Carmen Cruickshank: I think your page though is really good overall. What's interesting is we're seeing the same amount on computers and phones. But yeah, I think that's the first thing I'd change is just adding more buttons for mobile. Second thing I saw was keywords.

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:28.000
Noam: Okay, thank you.

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:54.000
Carmen Cruickshank: So overall on keywords for Google, I saw just for that one campaign, and I know you guys have one ad group in that campaign, we have 38 keywords. Normally, I'll have it maximum 15, but for me, 10 or less is ideal.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:48.000
Noam: Mmhm.

00:16:54.000 --> 00:17:04.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Because, basically, all these keywords, like, they're competing over one another. And, truly, what we can see is that only about 8.

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:56.000
Noam: Okay.

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:12.000
Carmen Cruickshank: are actually getting clicks. All the other ones are not getting clicks, so they're just kind of there, and sometimes they reduce the performance, so…

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:10.000
Noam: Yes.

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:19.000
Noam: But are they not getting clicks because we're getting, um, outbid… bidded? Or because people… there's no search intent? Like, what's the reason?

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:21.000
Carmen Cruickshank: I think it's just because…

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:21.000
Noam: That we're not getting.

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:31.000
Carmen Cruickshank: I think that we're not getting clicks on the extra keywords, just because normally what I'll see for all accounts that I've ever done Google Ads for is it's really only the top.

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:47.000
Carmen Cruickshank: 5 or 8 that actually are relevant to what people are searching for, and then the extra ones just kind of get put off. It's maybe too specific, or Google doesn't use that, show that the ad as much for that. I don't think it's anything wrong with you guys or anything. That's just like kind of a Google thing.

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:49.000
Noam: Okay.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:18:02.000
Carmen Cruickshank: But what I would do is honestly just like, I would pause anything that's not really getting clicked so far and just kind of have the 8 or 10. Something else I would also do, because I know you did mention spam.

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:08.000
Carmen Cruickshank: is I would change the match type to be phrase match instead of broad match.

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:13.000
Carmen Cruickshank: So, basically, with broad match, we could do…

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:19.000
Carmen Cruickshank: It kind of just attracts anyone and anything, so let's say I was doing Google Ads for, like.

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:28.000
Noam: Yeah, I'm familiar with it. I've done a few versions of this campaign, some were with exact match, some were with broad match, but when I did the exact match, it lowered… like, I had barely any impressions.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:33.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, no, you shouldn't do exact match. I think phrase match is good, because it's like, you're getting a new.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:30.000
Noam: Oh.

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:33.000
Noam: Oh, freeze magic.

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:34.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah. Okay.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:36.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Phrase match is just perfect.

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:42.000
Noam: Oh, it's another option! I didn't know… okay, sorry, I thought you mean exact match.

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:39.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yes.

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:55.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Oh, no, you're good. Yeah, if it was exact match, I'd be like, no, don't do that for me. Unless it was, like, a huge keyword, but that's rare. Uh, phrase match is just perfect in the middle. You get a good amount of searches, but it's not, like, all the spam.

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:56.000
Carmen Cruickshank: That's what I would recommend.

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:57.000
Noam: Okay, that's good to know.

00:18:57.000 --> 00:19:03.000
Carmen Cruickshank: And yeah, and then what else was it? I think the ad schedule is fine.

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:08.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Because unless you're getting leads in the middle of the night.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:09.000
Carmen Cruickshank: uh…

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:15.000
Carmen Cruickshank: So you noticed after you changed the schedule, though, the leads went down.

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:34.000
Noam: Yeah, because I used to get leads in the middle of the night from people, but I didn't really follow it because I was out of the country. So I got them in a time where I was awake, I was in Israel back then. So, I don't know what is exactly the right schedule, but I was hoping to have planners, even if they're in New York.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:24.000
Carmen Cruickshank: And…

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:28.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Oh.

